#: ../../src/struct/backup_spec.rst:18
msgid ""
"This is meant to provide a technical specification for the minimal syntax"
" of ``backup.json``, as read and written by :mod:`psp.serializers.json`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/struct/backup_spec.rst:24
msgid ""
"This isn't complete at the moment, so please refer to \"Backup File "
"Structure\" section from :ref:`basicproc` for a more detailed "
"explanation!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/struct/backup_spec.rst:29
msgid "Terminology"
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/struct/backup_spec.rst:31
msgid "Here are some terms that will be used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/struct/backup_spec.rst:40
msgid "attribute"
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/struct/backup_spec.rst:34
msgid ""
"An attribute is a pair of name and value, similar to key and value of a "
"Python *dict*.  For example the ``tz`` attribute (or more verbosely, the "
"value of the attribute with the name ``tz``) is a string and the ``data``"
" attribute of entries may be a *str* or *bool*.  To make it consistent I "
"will use code literals for attribute names (like ``tz`` and ``data``) and"
" italic for variables types (like *dict* and *str*) and names (like "
"*panels* and *entries*)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/struct/backup_spec.rst:43
msgid "field"
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/struct/backup_spec.rst:43
msgid "Another name for attribute (sometimes)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/struct/backup_spec.rst:49
msgid "*dict*, *list*, *str*, *bool*, null"
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/struct/backup_spec.rst:46
msgid ""
"These will be convenient Pythonic terms to refer to JSON objects, arrays,"
" strings, and booleans.  They are used mainly because object means "
"something different in Python; the use of null, however, is preserved, "
"despite in Python it is the singleton ``None``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/struct/backup_spec.rst:53
msgid "*text*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/struct/backup_spec.rst:52
msgid ""
"When an attribute is a *text* attribute, it must be either a *str* or a "
"*list* of *str* (such that ``''.join()`` can create a string from it)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/struct/backup_spec.rst:55
msgid ""
"Other terms such as \"panel\" and \"entry\" will be explained "
"progressively in the following text."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/struct/backup_spec.rst:61
msgid "Top-Level Attributes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/struct/backup_spec.rst:63
msgid ""
"A backup file is always a *dict*, inside which are what we will call the "
"*top-level attributes* and a *list* of *panels* stored under the key "
"``data``.  Here we will enumerate several keys (all surprisingly "
"optional) that you may use."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/struct/backup_spec.rst:72
msgid "tz (optional)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/struct/backup_spec.rst:69
msgid ""
"A *str* representing the time zone for everything in this backup. Must be"
" valid when passed to |parse_timezone|. This is optional but a time zone "
"must be eventually provided as |JSONLoader| parses some time/date time "
"string."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/struct/backup_spec.rst:83
msgid "paths (optional)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/struct/backup_spec.rst:75
msgid ""
"A *list* of *str* for the lookup paths.  Each time the ``input`` "
"attribute of an *entry* is parsed, its value is prepended with the "
"``base_dir`` option of |JSONLoader| and a path in this attribute."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/struct/backup_spec.rst:79
msgid ""
"By default this evaluates to simply ``['.']``---that is, the same "
"directory as ``base_dir``.  If this is not omitted, however, be noted "
"that ``\".\"`` will not be automatically added and you have to explicitly"
" add it if you want |JSONLoader| to look in the same directory as "
"``base_dir``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/struct/backup_spec.rst:88
msgid "data (optional)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/struct/backup_spec.rst:86
msgid ""
"A *list* of *dict*, each *dict* being what is called a *panel*.  The "
"content of each *dict* is elaborated in the following section. An empty "
"list is assumed if this is omitted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/struct/backup_spec.rst:90
msgid ""
"Any other key is ignored by |JSONLoader|, though there is one key that is"
" recommended for you to use.  It is also addressed because |JSONDumper| "
"exports it and the ``psp synopsis`` command recognizes it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/struct/backup_spec.rst:99
msgid "desc (optional)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/struct/backup_spec.rst:95
msgid ""
"A *text* attribute giving a brief description of this backup file. This "
"is just a recommendation previously reinforced by :mod:`basicproc` and, "
"sometimes, other \"nonstandard\" parts of my code.  |JSONLoader| never "
"tries to parse this."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/struct/backup_spec.rst:103
msgid "Panels"
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/struct/backup_spec.rst:105
msgid ""
"Now for the panels!  A *panel* is a container of *entries*, loosely "
"speaking. It does cooler stuff than that though, but first let's talk "
"about the one and only **required** attribute:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/struct/backup_spec.rst:111
msgid "date"
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/struct/backup_spec.rst:110
msgid ""
"A *str* representing the date of the panel.  Must be valid when passed to"
" |parse_date|."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/struct/backup_spec.rst:113
msgid "For providing entries:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/struct/backup_spec.rst:118
msgid "entries (optional)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/struct/backup_spec.rst:116
msgid ""
"A *list* of *dict*, each *dict* being what is called an *entry*. The "
"content of each *dict* is elaborated in the following section. An empty "
"list is assumed if this is omitted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/struct/backup_spec.rst:120
msgid "There is only one valid optional attribute:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/struct/backup_spec.rst:159
msgid "rating (optional)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/struct/backup_spec.rst:123
msgid ""
"A *str* representing the rating of the panel (can be null). The three "
"ratings from Perspective from bad to good are represented with the "
"strings ``\":(\"``, ``\":|\"``, and ``\":)\"``. (I did not use numbers "
"because I'm not a nerd >_> (well, not entirely))"
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/struct/backup_spec.rst:128
msgid "Rating is set to null when omitted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/struct/backup_spec.rst:130
msgid "Example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/struct/backup_spec.rst:163
msgid "Entries"
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/struct/backup_spec.rst:165
msgid ""
"Now for the entries... this can get tricky since this is where most of "
"the things take place."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/struct/backup_spec.rst:173
msgid "Inference"
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/struct/backup_spec.rst:177
msgid ""
"This will be a reorganized version of the algorithm from :ref:`basicproc "
"<basicproc_inference>`."
msgstr ""

